+# PR draft — chưa gửi GitHub
+
+**Title:** `fix(sprint1): isolate login IP budgets and recover organizer event editing`
+
+Sprint1 login lacked an IP failure budget, organizer times depended on the device timezone, and expired sessions left the event form unable to recover. Add Redis IP limits with an authenticated transport-peer boundary through the web proxy, explicit Vietnam event times, and login return/draft recovery for the same user. Keep V1 presentation and the existing five-failure/15-minute account contract.
+
+Provide a guarded, isolated PowerShell demo profile, fake accounts, real API/browser regression and Docker runtime packaging for the custom web entry. Preserve existing migrations, source/WIP and data. New server-only `AUTH_PROXY_SECRET` must match web/API; `WEB_PORT` separates the web from API port. Use the supported web entry, not bare next start.
+
+Validation: Node24.21.0/pnpm10.15.1 frozen install; targeted format, lint/typecheck/build;238unit tests;109integration tests over two guarded isolated profiles;15desktop/mobile browser checks; real API/Redis lock/restart/natural900s expiry; proxy multi-peer/spoof checks; dependency health503/recovery; compensating migration cycle; Docker runtime smoke. See Sprint1 report/matrix and exact source manifest.
+
+**Not ready to publish:** dependency audit has12 unresolved advisory signals; finalSHA remoteCI and independent review absent; staging deploy/rollback/client-IP edge and AC/DoD remain BLOCKED. Source mainCI is evidence for81d1dd9 only. No deployment or new Sprint scope implied. Resolve these gates before publishing.
+
+Rollback: stop owned local processes, preserve data; future code revert through reviewed PR. No product migration changed. Never reset shared database, regenerate existing signing keys or disable guards to recover demo.
